# ── SECURITY CONTROL, not build hygiene ─────────────────────────────────────
# The repo root contains .env with REAL API keys (GOOGLE_API_KEY,
# DEEPSEEK_API_KEY). Without this line, a `COPY . .` would bake those keys
# into an image layer; anyone who can pull the image can extract that layer
# and read the keys. .env must never exist in any image, ever.
.env
# Any .env variant (.env.local, .env.production, ...) gets the same
# treatment — assume any of them may hold secrets.
.env.*
# ...with ONE deliberate exception: .env.example is committed and contains
# documented placeholder NAMES only, no real values. Excluding it would
# falsely signal to a reader that it holds secrets.
!.env.example
# .git would double the build context and leak the repo's full history into
# an image layer.
.git
# data/ holds the live local SQLite database — a database must never ship
# inside an image (it would be stale by definition, and in deployment the
# database is Cloud SQL, not a file).
data/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
# Tests and docs are dev-time artifacts; the console image runs none of
# them, so they would only bloat the context and the image.
tests/
docs/
*.db
# Local virtualenvs would shadow the image's own site-packages if copied.
.venv/
venv/
